msgid "REST Client and RESTEasy interactions"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"In Quarkus, the REST Client extension and xref:rest-json.adoc[the RESTEasy "
"extension] share the same infrastructure.\n"
"One important consequence of this consideration is that they share the same "
"list of providers (in the JAX-RS meaning of the word)."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"For instance, if you declare a `WriterInterceptor`, it will by default "
"intercept both the servers calls and the client calls,\n"
"which might not be the desired behavior."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"However, you can change this default behavior and constrain a provider to:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"only consider *client* calls by adding the `@ConstrainedTo(RuntimeType."
"CLIENT)` annotation to your provider;"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"only consider *server* calls by adding the `@ConstrainedTo(RuntimeType."
"SERVER)` annotation to your provider."
msgstr ""

msgid "Using a Mock HTTP Server for tests"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Setting up a mock HTTP server, against which tests are run, is a common "
"testing pattern.\n"
"Examples of such servers are link:https://wiremock.org/[Wiremock] and link:"
"https://docs.hoverfly.io/projects/hoverfly-java/en/latest/index."
"html[Hoverfly].\n"
"In this section we'll demonstrate how Wiremock can be leveraged for testing "
"the `ExtensionsService` which was developed above."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"First, Wiremock needs to be added as a test dependency. For a Maven project "
"that would happen like so:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Use a proper Wiremock version. All available versions can be found link:"
"https://search.maven.org/artifact/com.github.tomakehurst/wiremock-jre8[here]."
""
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"In Quarkus tests when some service needs to be started before the Quarkus "
"tests are ran, we utilize the `@io.quarkus.test.common.QuarkusTestResource`\n"
"annotation to specify a `io.quarkus.test.common."
"QuarkusTestResourceLifecycleManager` which can start the service and supply "
"configuration\n"
"values that Quarkus will use."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"For more details about `@QuarkusTestResource` refer to  xref:getting-started-"
"testing.adoc#quarkus-test-resource[this part of the documentation]."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Let's create an implementation of `QuarkusTestResourceLifecycleManager` "
"called `WiremockExtensions` like so:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Statically importing the methods in the Wiremock package makes it easier to "
"read the test."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The `start` method is invoked by Quarkus before any test is run and returns "
"a `Map` of configuration properties that apply during the test execution."
msgstr ""

msgid "Launch Wiremock."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Configure Wiremock to stub the calls to `/extensions?id=io.quarkus:quarkus-"
"rest-client` by returning a specific canned response."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"All HTTP calls that have not been stubbed are handled by calling the real "
"service. This is done for demonstration purposes, as it is not something "
"that would usually happen in a real test."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"As the `start` method returns configuration that applies for tests, we set "
"the rest-client property that controls the base URL which is used by the "
"implementation\n"
"of `ExtensionsService` to the base URL where Wiremock is listening for "
"incoming requests."
msgstr ""

